{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2"],"primary":"c1","title":"Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance (RSO) - allowable annual rent increases","requirement":"Rent for RSO units may be increased only once every 12 months, by no more than the allowable percentage published annually by LAHD. Since February 2, 2026 landlords may not add any extra percentage for utilities. Increases above the allowable percentage require LAHD approval, except for permitted pass-through surcharges and market-rate resets on qualifying vacancy events.","key_value":"One increase per 12 months, capped at the LAHD-published allowable percentage. The rate was 3% for 2025-07-01 through 2026-06-30. The sources do not state the rate for the period from 2026-07-01. No utility add-on since 2026-02-02.","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance (Los Angeles Municipal Code)","coverage_conditions":"Rental properties first built on or before October 1, 1978, plus replacement units under LAMC Section 151.28. Covered unit types: apartments, condominiums, townhomes, duplexes, and two or more single-family units on one parcel. Also covered: hotel, motel and rooming-house rooms occupied by the same tenant for more than 30 consecutive days; residential units attached to commercial buildings; ADUs; JADUs; and mobile homes and RVs in mobile home parks.","exemptions":"Rent amount is not regulated for condominium or townhome tenancies that began after December 31, 1995. Landlords can apply for a Luxury Exemption. Temporary exemptions also exist.","conflict_note":"The two sources do not conflict on the rule itself. D042 (c2) gives a 3% allowable increase only for 2025-07-01 through 2026-06-30, a period that ended before the 2026-10-01 reference date. D041 (c1) does not state any percentage. Neither source gives the currently applicable rate. On the registration (RSO) surcharge, D041 (c1) shows both $1.61 and $38.75, while D042 (c2) states $1.61/month. The $1.61/month figure is better supported."}],"dropped":[]}
